# Session fix (global)

Apply only the **fix now** items from a session review. This is not a feature pass and not the next-session itinerary.

## Start from a review

If this chat already has a **fix now** list, use that list.

If it does not, read `agents/prompts/session-review.md`, run that review, then fix only what landed in **fix now**.

Leave **next session** items untouched, including anything the brain dump wants to focus on next.

## How to change the code

- One concern at a time. Stop if a "quick" fix starts needing a product decision, a schema change, or a new dependency — move it to **next session** and say so.
- Match the surrounding code. Read `AGENTS.md` in the directories you touch.
- Add or adjust a test when the fix changes behavior. Skip a new test only when the fix is non-behavioral (a typo, an unused import, a comment).
- Verify with the narrowest check that covers the edit (`npm run type-check`, the relevant test file, or both).

When you finish, list what you changed and what remains for `/session-next`. Do not write the itinerary here unless they also asked for it. Do not commit unless they ask.
